  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women and Energy Fund - NBS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women Energy Fund is sustaining the gains achieved by the &#x2018;Breaking the Barriers&#x2019; 42-month multi-country project which worked to promote women entrepreneurship in the sustainable energy sector. In Malawi, the project is supporting Women-Led Sustainable Energy Enterprises (WLSEEs) in food processing businesses in the rice, fish, and horticultural value chains.
Activities:
- Women-only groups organized and structured into WLSEEs.
- Technical support and capacity building.
- Provision of financial support to WLSEES by the means of a grant (70%) and loan (25%), with the WLSEEs themselves contributing 5%.
- Awareness raising and advocacy.</narrative>
  </description>
